[Classical Art Museums: Genuine Masterpieces > Old Masters Art Gallery: Superstars of the Renaissance]

Almost every visitor to Dresden has the Zwinger on their itinerary. No wonder, since the impressive building complex is one of Germany's most important baroque buildings. Not to mention the interior features! The Old Masters Art Gallery housed here is one of the most renowned collections of paintings in the world. The "Who's Who" of painting, from Peter Paul Rubens to Albrecht Dürer, is gathered across three floors, focusing in particular on the Renaissance period.&#x20;

